The resulting architecture is not fundamentally a stock predictor.

It is not fundamentally a trading strategy.

It is not fundamentally a neural network.

It is not fundamentally a simulator.

It is a **general-purpose calculus for deciding how an intelligent system should intervene in a dynamic world under uncertainty and constraints**.

The economic market is its first major domain.

The deeper theory is broader:

> **Observe reality. Construct uncertainty. Generate transformations. Prove validity. Explore possible futures. Intervene only within the feasible space. Measure the consequence. Learn from the divergence. Repeat.**

That is WORLD // NEXUS.

The mathematics of **WORLD // NEXUS** is best understood not as one giant financial equation, but as a **stack of mathematical theories that describe what the system can know, what can happen, what it may do, and how it learns from the consequences**.

The important conceptual shift is this:

> **The system is not primarily a price predictor. It is a mathematical engine for discovering, verifying, executing, and evaluating interventions in a partially observed dynamical economic system.**

